WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.917
St0r — a modern management interface for UrBackup

2
00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:12.528
For administrators who already run UrBackup Server. It does not replace the backup engine.

3
00:00:12.528 --> 00:00:17.336
The dashboard: every endpoint, job totals, replication health and capacity in one view

4
00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:24.018
Three backups are running right now, with live progress

5
00:00:27.041 --> 00:00:31.251
And one endpoint needs attention — surfaced instead of buried

6
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.191
Workflow one: every endpoint, its customer, last backup and quota usage

7
00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:46.933
Filter by state or by customer to find what you are looking for

8
00:00:50.694 --> 00:00:55.107
Opening an endpoint shows its status and full backup history

9
00:01:03.336 --> 00:01:07.746
Workflow two: recovering a file. Pick a day that has a backup

10
00:01:15.228 --> 00:01:18.839
Open the backup taken that day

11
00:01:21.964 --> 00:01:26.574
Browse into the backup and download individual files or whole folders

12
00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:44.028
Workflow three: schedules and retention, per endpoint

13
00:01:46.764 --> 00:01:51.977
Intervals, backup windows and how many snapshots to keep — with UrBackup defaults shown

14
00:01:57.115 --> 00:02:01.124
And an optional storage quota with warning thresholds

15
00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:05.342
St0r ships light and dark themes

16
00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:12.242
Replication: target health, lag, and the history of every run

17
00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:26.017
Each run records status, trigger, duration and bytes transferred

18
00:02:32.832 --> 00:02:37.640
Reports summarise the estate and export to CSV or PDF

19
00:02:44.928 --> 00:02:49.740
Alerts raise failures and stale backups on the channels you choose

20
00:02:56.151 --> 00:03:00.357
For MSPs: group endpoints by customer …

21
00:03:03.762 --> 00:03:08.772
… then scope a read-only account to just that customer's endpoints

22
00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.666
Install with one command on the same server as UrBackup
